---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { repo, url } from "../lib/site";

const features = [
  {
    title: "JDKs from 20+ vendors",
    text: "Temurin, Corretto, Zulu, Liberica, Oracle, GraalVM, SapMachine, Semeru, Microsoft and more, from the foojay Disco API. Pick one per install or set a default.",
  },
  {
    title: "Maven and Gradle too",
    text: "Straight from Maven Central and services.gradle.org. Projects that use ./mvnw or ./gradlew keep their wrapper; jkit supplies the JDK.",
  },
  {
    title: "No JDK needed to run",
    text: "A single native binary built with GraalVM. Starts in milliseconds, so it can run from your shell prompt without slowing it down.",
  },
  {
    title: "Switch per shell or globally",
    text: "jkit use jdk@21 changes this shell only; --global changes the default for every terminal and app. jkit reset goes back.",
  },
  {
    title: "Checked downloads",
    text: "Every archive is checked against the checksum its source publishes before anything is unpacked. A failed install leaves nothing behind.",
  },
  {
    title: "A GraalVM slot",
    text: "Keep Temurin as JAVA_HOME and point GRAALVM_HOME at GraalVM for native-image builds: jkit use graalvm@25.",
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="badge">v0.1.0 · Linux x64 and arm64</p>
        <h1>Install and switch JDKs, Maven and Gradle.</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          jkit is one small native command for Linux, macOS and Windows. Name a version, and an
          optional vendor, and it does the rest. No bash scripts, no JDK required.
        </p>
        <p class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href={url("install")}>Install jkit</a>
          <a class="btn" href={url("docs")}>Read the docs</a>
          <a class="btn" href={repo}>GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <pre class="term" aria-label="Example terminal session"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit install jdk@21</span>
<span class="dim">downloading jdk 21.0.13+9 temurin from github.com</span>
installed jdk 21.0.13+9 temurin
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit install jdk@17 zulu</span>
installed jdk 17.0.21+9 zulu
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit use jdk@21 --global</span>
global jdk → 21.0.13+9 temurin
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit use jdk@17 zulu</span>
using jdk 17.0.21+9 zulu in this shell
<span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">java -version</span>
openjdk version "17.0.21" 2026-10-20 LTS</pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {features.map((f) => (
        <article class="card">
          <h3>{f.title}</h3>
          <p>{f.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Every major version, at a glance</h2>
    <p>
      <code>jkit search jdk</code> shows one row per major version: your default vendor's newest
      build in the middle, and who else ships it.
    </p>
    <pre class="term"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="cmd">jkit search jdk --maintained</span>
major      temurin *       also from
27         27.0.1.1+4      corretto liberica openjdk oracle sapmachine semeru +1
25    LTS  25.0.5+8        bisheng corretto dragonwell eliya graalvm +14
21    LTS  21.0.13+9 ●     bisheng corretto dragonwell gluon-graalvm graalvm +14
17    LTS  17.0.21+9       bisheng corretto dragonwell graalvm graalvm-ce +13
11    LTS  11.0.33+10      bisheng corretto dragonwell jetbrains kona +12
8     LTS  8.0.512+9       bisheng corretto dragonwell kona liberica openjdk +4
<span class="dim">* default vendor   ● installed   eol = no longer maintained</span></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Why not SDKMAN?</h2>
    <p>
      SDKMAN is great, but it is written in bash, so on Windows it needs WSL or Git Bash. jkit is a
      native binary on every platform, with its own command design: version ranges like
      <code>jdk@21</code>, an optional vendor instead of IDs like <code>21.0.5-tem</code>, no
      interactive prompts, and a clear difference between this shell and the global default.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap status">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p class="note">
      jkit is a working prototype. <code>search</code>, <code>install</code>, <code>use</code>,
      <code>reset</code>, <code>list</code>, <code>remove</code> and the shell hook work and are
      tested on Linux. Project files (<code>jkit.toml</code>, <code>jkit.lock</code>),
      <code>status</code>, <code>doctor</code>, self-update, and Windows and macOS testing are
      next. See the <a href={url("docs")}>docs</a> for the full list.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { background: var(--bg-soft); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 48px 0; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; align-items: center; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem); margin: 0.3em 0; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.15em; color: var(--muted); }
  .badge {
    display: inline-block; margin: 0; padding: 2px 10px; border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .ctas { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5em; }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block; padding: 9px 16px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; background: var(--bg);
  }
  .btn:hover { text-decoration: none; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  .term { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 4px 18px 8px; background: var(--bg); }
  .card h3 { font-size: 1.05em; margin-bottom: 0.3em; }
  .card p { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 0; }
  .status { padding-bottom: 48px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
